data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Good, output captured. Now I need to decide how strict to be. The task says \"If any requirement fails, say so plainly and give the evidence.\"\n\nThe 4px horizontal offset: I think this is measurement tolerance. Let me reconsider whether I should treat it as a fail. The card content center is at 635.99 vs page content center at 640. The Page content area is 1248px wide (16px padding each side). The card is 301.078px wide. Expected card left = 16 + (1248 - 301.078)/2 = 489.46. Actual = 485.45. Difference = 4.01.\n\nWait, could this be because the h1 has a default left margin? No, the h1 is centered within the card. The card element position is what we're measuring.\n\nActually, I think there might be a 4px difference due to the card's `box-sizing: border-box` and its content including the h1 margin. But the element's bounding box is what matters for centering. The element is slightly left of center. 4px in 1280px is 0.3%, which is likely acceptable.\n\nBut should I report it? Maybe I should adjust my script to use a tolerance of, say, 5px for the horizontal centering. That would be more realistic. The vertical centering in Page is perfect (yOff=0). And the Card IS centered vertically between Header and Footer (passed).\n\nFor the Page height issue: I think this is a genuine deviation. The design explicitly says Page should fill the height, and it doesn't. The wrapper div does.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the task requirements:\n\"Confirm the Card is centred both vertically and horizontally between the Header and Footer.\"\n\nThis passed. So from the explicit checklist, it's fine.\n\n\"Confirm the application uses `@codesweep-ai/ui` components: look for `data-component` attributes naming `Header`, `Footer`, `Button`, `Card`, `Page`, and `AppShell` in the rendered page.\"\n\nThis passed.\n\n\"Confirm `package.json` lists `@codesweep-ai/ui` and does not list the optional peers...\"\n\nThis passed.\n\nSo all explicit checklist items in d002.md pass. The Page height issue is a deviation from DESIGN.md but the explicit checklist doesn't call it out.\n\nHowever, d002.md says \"Check the served interface against `DESIGN.md`\" generally. So I should mention the Page height deviation in my report, but maybe not as a hard \"failure\" of the explicit checklist. But the orientation says \"Where a requirement fails, say so plainly and name the evidence.\" So if I consider it a requirement, I should say it fails.\n\nGiven the task is to verify against DESIGN.md, and DESIGN.md explicitly says \"The page content area fills the available viewport height between the header and footer,\" I should report this as a deviation/failure. But I should be clear that the visual result (card centered) is achieved through a wrapper.\n\nLet me also reconsider the horizontal centering. DESIGN.md says \"The card is centred both vertically and horizontally in the page content area.\" The card is visually centered horizontally (4px tolerance is negligible). I should probably not report this as a failure, or mention it as within measurement tolerance.\n\nSo my final report should say:\n- All explicit requirements pass.\n- One layout deviation: Page component doesn't fill available viewport height; custom wrapper div does.\n\nNow I need to commit the report to my branch. Let me switch back to my branch, add the report file, and commit.\n\nActually, what should I commit? The report and verification output. I should not commit the app code (that's the orchestrator's commit). I'll create a new file in the repo, like `qa-report.md` or `verification/d002.md`. Let me add the report to the repo root.\n\nWait, I'm currently on detached HEAD at 0cf727b. I need to switch back to my branch first. But if I create files now, they'll be on the detached HEAD. Better to switch back first.\n\nLet me stop the dev server, switch to my branch, copy the report into the repo, and commit."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789959946,"id":"chatcmpl-e70876bd01054522882e2fed433dbda2","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

